    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/billings-mt#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide electronics recycling in Billings, MT?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS Electronic Recycling provides certified processing electronics recycling and ITAD services throughout Billings and Yellowstone County. We serve businesses, healthcare systems, energy-sector offices, government agencies, and educational institutions across the greater Billings region, including downtown, the West End, Billings Heights, Lockwood, and Laurel. Our secure fleet offers free pickup for qualifying volumes near I-90 and I-94, and all equipment is processed at our 200,000 sq ft certified processing facility with NIST 800-88 compliant data sanitization and complete chain-of-custody documentation for Yellowstone County organizations."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is your data destruction HIPAA compliant for Billings healthcare facilities?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS supports HIPAA compliance for Billings healthcare organizations including Billings Clinic and St. Vincent Healthcare. Under HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312, electronic protected health information on disposed devices must be rendered irretrievable. Our secure data destruction meets and exceeds NIST 800-88 purge and destroy standards, and every engagement includes PHI chain-of-custody validation and certificates of destruction for OCR audit preparation. Healthcare clients throughout Yellowstone County receive documentation that supports HIPAA audits along with off-hours pickup coordination to avoid disruption to clinical operations."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free in the Billings area?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Free pickup is available throughout Billings and Yellowstone County for qualifying volumes, with no hidden fees. Our secure fleet collects equipment from single offices to enterprise data centers serving downtown Billings, the West End, Heights, Lockwood, Laurel, and surrounding communities near I-90 and I-94. For larger projects, asset recovery credits from remarketed equipment can further offset processing costs. Scheduling is flexible, and most Billings organizations receive same-week response. Contact our team at 844-699-2913 to confirm coverage and arrange a convenient pickup window for your location."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications does STS hold?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS holds certified processing (secure recycling) certification for electronics recycling and secure data destruction certification for data destruction. Our destruction processes are NIST 800-88 compliant, and we maintain HIPAA-aligned workflows for healthcare clients throughout Billings and Yellowstone County. certified processing certification ensures downstream tracking through final processing at certified smelters with third-party auditing, while secure data destruction certification is verified through unannounced audits. Together these credentials support federal and Montana state requirements for healthcare systems, energy-sector firms, government agencies, and educational institutions retiring data-bearing equipment in the Billings region."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How quickly can you schedule a pickup in Billings?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most Billings organizations receive same-week response after requesting a quote. STS offers flexible scheduling for businesses, healthcare facilities, and government agencies throughout Yellowstone County, with pickup windows arranged around your operating hours. Energy-sector and corporate clients often coordinate scheduled pickups to avoid business interruption, while healthcare clients can arrange off-hours service. To begin, call 844-699-2913 or submit the online quote form with your equipment types, quantities, and preferred timing. Our team confirms logistics for your Billings location and provides chain-of-custody documentation from the first point of collection."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you serve government agencies and schools in Yellowstone County?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS provides certified processing data destruction and electronics recycling for Yellowstone County offices, Billings Public Schools, and federal field offices including BLM and USFS. Government and education clients receive chain-of-custody reporting and NIST 800-88 compliant destruction that supports procurement and FERPA requirements. We coordinate multi-building pickups across the Billings area and provide asset reports suitable for administrative and board review. Educational institutions such as Montana State University Billings and Rocky Mountain College schedule around academic calendars, and all retired equipment is processed with complete documentation throughout Yellowstone County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to my equipment after pickup from Billings?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "After pickup from your Billings location, equipment is transported under documented chain-of-custody to our 200,000 sq ft certified processing facility. Data-bearing devices undergo NIST 800-88 compliant sanitization or physical destruction, then materials are recovered through certified processing downstream processing with zero landfill. Functional assets may be securely wiped and remarketed for value recovery. Throughout the process, serial-level tracking documents each device, and Billings organizations receive certificates of destruction detailing methods, weights, and downstream facilities to support HIPAA, NIST 800-88, and audit requirements across Yellowstone County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can Billings businesses recover value from retired IT equipment?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS asset remarketing helps Billings businesses recover value from computers, laptops, LCD monitors, and other retired IT equipment through secure, certified processing disposition. Functional assets are securely wiped to NIST 800-88 standards, then evaluated for remarketing, with recovery credits that can offset processing and pickup costs for larger projects. Energy-sector firms, healthcare systems, and corporate offices throughout Yellowstone County use this service to balance compliance with cost recovery. To discover your equipment's value, call 844-699-2913 or email recycle@stsrecycle.com for a no-obligation assessment of your Billings IT assets."
          }
        }
      ]
